# Who must approve a pull request (CONTRIBUTING.md, "Review and merging").
#
# The "main" ruleset requires a code owner's approval, and GitHub does not let an author approve their own pull
# request. So a change to an owned path merges only with the approval of the maintainer who did not write it, and a
# contributor's change with the approval of either. The last matching line wins.
#
# Everything is owned unless a later line says otherwise: readings, keys, transcriptions, the catalogue, leads,
# credits, write-up pages, the checkers, the build scripts, the workflows and this file.
